# The same proof with one generator serving two withheld messages.
#
# The draft forbids this, in a sentence that states both halves of
# what our criterion decides: "The generators MUST be unique and
# pseudo-random i.e., with no known relationship to each other"
# (section 3.3).  Uniqueness is the half a checker reading the
# relation can decide, and this file is what its failure looks like --
# the two withheld messages trade against each other, so the proof
# pins only their sum.  It is the credential relation of
# credential-broken.rel, reached in a different decade by a different
# committee.
#
# "No known relationship" is the other half, and our completeness
# theorem says no checker reading the relation can decide it: seeing
# that H_j1 and H_j2 are related means computing a discrete logarithm.
# The draft asks for it as a construction requirement rather than a
# check, which is the only place it can live.
secrets e r1 r3 m_j1 m_j2
claims  e r1 r3 m_j1 m_j2
eq  Bbar   Abar  D   1  1   1
eq  Bv     1     1   D  H   H
